  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1245 PM CDT Sat Aug 1 2026\n\nWhat a pleasant day! Temperatures are mostly in the upper 70s\nwith dewpoints in the reasonable mid-60s. Northerly winds are \ntoo gusty for my taste with 15-25 mph blasts of air common. The \nH5 pattern shows cloud cover just southeast of the area, tied to\na cutoff low spinning over Illinois. A few fair weather cumulus\nat 2500 ft can be spotted on GOES-19.\n\nSkies are expected to remain mostly *cloud-free* over the next \n36 hours, but will be polluted with wildfire smoke wafting in \nfrom the north. Have added 20-30% sky cover to the grids to \nrepresent the elevated smoke and reduced insolation. Under the \n\"clear\" skies tonight, temps will fall to mid-50s to near 60 and\nthen afternoon highs will push a bit higher than Saturday, \nclimbing into the mid-80s.\n\nI've also introduced patchy fog to the forecast tonight as \nwinds are expected to abate overnight as the aforementioned \nupper low loses influence on the region and before southerly \nreturn flow develops for Sunday. Fog is likeliest in low-lying \nareas and in northeast Nebraska. It should burn off by 9am.",
